 # Working notes: 6595a30d2676
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## 2026-10-25 peer repair: restore the generator contract
+
+### Defect
+
+The inherited generator advertised controls that were not dependable.  In
+particular, `frame_side` was accepted but ignored, unknown override keys were
+silently accepted, several declared controls were dead or only partly honored,
+and there were no task-local regression tests.  A source-bound baseline override
+probe found 1,897 findings across 43,830 draws, including override mismatches,
+generation errors, invalid grids, missing axis provenance, and an unknown-key
+contract failure.
+
+### Repair
+
+Version 3.1.0 now exposes exactly four observable axes:
+
+- `grid_h`: 9..28
+- `grid_w`: 9..28
+- `n_frames`: 1..5
+- `frame_side`: 5, 7, or 9
+
+Unknown keys, booleans, invalid values, and impossible requests fail closed.
+Feasible multi-axis requests are honored exactly.  Deterministic shelf packing
+keeps frames separated and makes every reported axis recoverable from the grid.
+The default schedule retains all canonical dimension/palette profiles, and a
+Python mirror is checked against every official label while Racket remains the
+authority.
+
+Every three consecutive default examples expose all four rotation keys.  Five
+executable lesson competitors cover fixed identity/quarter/half/three-quarter
+turns and reversed key direction.  They are correctly declared as
+`LESSON_COMPETITORS`, not `CANONICAL_SHORTCUTS`, because none fits all four
+canonical labels.  The three-demo identifiability hook rejects any surviving
+competitor.
+
+### Verification
+
+- Original generator SHA-256:
+  `2391904041b3d27d7c511ca215afd7331ab45ff852c60f5836cf01694eeb09d0`
+- Repaired generator SHA-256:
+  `456f8f6f26fafb468441e6913b976dc3132c3f12f7b90122dab235a8cf6b3025`
+- Canonical rule hash: `de3e88d65417` (authority unchanged)
+- Fresh task-local tests: 10/10 passed
+- Native battery: all 12 stages green (lint, self-check, rule smoke, defect
+  lint, distribution, profile floor, semantic gate, diversity, override,
+  grammar, Racket lint, and authority sync)
+
+The repair is reviewer-side peer work.  Owner checked integration is still
+required; no parametric acceptance or training admission is claimed.
